{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Serve the inventory application on node1 over TCP port 8181.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Apache was active and listening on all interfaces at TCP 8181, and an HTTP request to node1 returned the inventory application content. The same behavior was directly verified after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e8863999c8814802","cmd-4a53b719b87a4100","cmd-263a75a8084a4b22","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep the system's mandatory access control in enforcing mode while serving the application.","status":"satisfied","summary":"AppArmor was loaded with 24 profiles in enforce mode before changes, while the application was serving, and after reboot; the AppArmor service was also active afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-17726892d57d4d35","cmd-e8863999c8814802","cmd-4a53b719b87a4100","cmd-263a75a8084a4b22"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS with kernel 6.8.0-71-generic across execution and reboot. Apache 2.4.58 was installed from the Ubuntu Noble package repositories, providing direct evidence of platform-compatible software.","evidence_ids":["cmd-17726892d57d4d35","cmd-6bb3a65f8d394f20","cmd-263a75a8084a4b22","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing Apache and updating package metadata were necessary prerequisites (cmd-ec71dbd128ef4a74); changing its port and virtual host, writing the application page, restarting it, and enabling it for recovery directly supported the outcome (cmd-6ac1ea510cc24103). The transient reboot unit was required by the provider-wide restart protocol and did not persist after reboot (cmd-bd4e87cc02934ca9). Temporary installation tracking files were absent from the final bounded /tmp inventory. Final package state was healthy and no failed services were present; the only new listening service was the required Apache endpoint on 8181.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ec71dbd128ef4a74","cmd-6ac1ea510cc24103","cmd-bd4e87cc02934ca9","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The independent node-restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, the restart was acknowledged, its boot ID changed from 242af11e-49fb-4e07-a001-8016b2349acb to 6b20b114-17f5-4cbd-a273-7400b80fa1a3, and the service, application response, port, operating-system state, and AppArmor enforcement recovered. Fixed lifecycle observations independently corroborate the boot transition and final healthy state.","limitations":["The evidence demonstrates the specified inventory response but does not test application behavior beyond that single HTTP endpoint; no richer inventory functionality was defined by the task.","AppArmor evidence establishes that the system framework remained active with enforcing profiles, but it does not claim or demonstrate that Apache itself has a dedicated AppArmor profile; the public instruction did not explicitly require that additional confinement."]}
